// Returning an owned string (`own *string`) as a borrowed `string` would
// dangle: `s` owns its buffer and is freed when `view` returns, so the caller
// would observe a use-after-free. The function must declare its return type as
// `own *string` to transfer ownership instead. (Applies equally to an owned
// local or a concat temporary coerced down to `string`.)
string view(own *string s) { return s; }
unit main() {
  own *string o = "hi" + "!";
  log(view(o));
}
